            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary artery stenting. A new therapeutic alternative in Norway].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1429-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In Norway the first percutaneously, transluminally placed human coronary artery endoprosthesis (stent) was implanted in the spring of 1991. This article summarizes international experience of treatment with the Palmaz-Schatz balloon expandable stent for coronary use and describes the first two patients treated with such implants at Ullevål hospital.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
